from pathlib import Path
import json
import pandas as pd
R=Path('output/evaluation-enriched');A=R/'analysis'
def table(headers,rows):
 return '\n'.join(['| '+' | '.join(headers)+' |','| '+' | '.join(['---']*len(headers))+' |']+['| '+' | '.join(str(x) for x in row)+' |' for row in rows])
def main():
 s=pd.read_csv(A/'model_summary.csv');c=pd.read_csv(A/'comparison_uncertainty.csv');ab=pd.read_csv(A/'ablation_uncertainty.csv');meta=json.loads((R/'protocol.json').read_text());res=json.loads((A/'summary.json').read_text())
 tasks=['conditional_points','overall_points','participation','minutes'];labels={'conditional_points':'Conditional points MAE','overall_points':'Overall points MAE','participation':'Participation Brier','minutes':'Minutes MAE'}
 def get(config,task):return s[(s.configuration==config)&(s.task==task)].iloc[0]
 rows=[]
 for task in tasks:
  old=get('reduced_matched',task).loss;new=get('full',task).loss;rows.append([labels[task],f'{old:.5f}',f'{new:.5f}',f'{100*(old-new)/old:.2f}%'])
 text=['# Updated historical ML evaluation with recovered features','Completed 15 September 2026. This report is the current technical ML summary. The earlier Day 1-4, component and uncertainty reports remain valid records of the reduced 16-feature experiment. They are not overwritten.','## What was redone','The data audit was extended to archived metadata; training and evaluation features were rebuilt; the reduced model was reproduced on matched cases; the enriched model was evaluated over all 15 gameweeks; error analysis and calibration were regenerated; nine feature-group ablations were run; and paired uncertainty estimates were recalculated. These changes concern ML evaluation, not UI sessions, scoring equations, recommendations or chatbot quality.','## Data and validation','We now hold 36 pinned historical captures: GW1-35 provide historical context and target-time metadata, while GW36 supports checking the final target outcomes. Hashes were checked against manifests, capture timestamps were checked against the deadlines inside payloads, the intended target had to be marked as next, and all earlier gameweeks had to be marked finished. A direct fetch of the original GW21 Internet Archive response matched the archived hash. Other captures were checked against their repository manifests; original Wayback responses were not all independently fetched.','The repository revision is f8735a02e5c4abb018521f241340429c906d23ae. Local cumulative points and minutes matched the API totals for all overlapping players through pre-GW36. This corroborates the outcome data but is not an audit of every fixture or collection process. The snapshot player code is consistent within each player ID across captures. Short-name variants remain metadata, not model features.',f'No previously eligible training or test rows were excluded by the snapshot join. The full and reduced configurations therefore evaluate the same {res["n"]:,} player-gameweek rows, {res["unique_players"]} players and {res["qualifying"]:,} qualifying appearances (at least 30 minutes). Target rounds remain GW21-35 of the stored 2025-26 season.','## The 38-feature configuration','The original 16 player-history features are retained. Added groups: price and ownership (2); availability/status and chance-of-playing with missingness (8); archived API form (1); position indicators (4); and seven archived team-strength measures (7). IDs, names and team IDs are used for joining only, not numeric predictors.','Chance-of-playing nulls remain missing and have an explicit indicator; median imputation is fitted only on training rows. They are not silently treated as zero or 100%. Prices use millions and ownership uses proportions. Metadata is taken from the last selected archived capture before the deadline, which may be several hours old; it is not claimed to be the final deadline value.','Training uses the same gradient boosting and XGBoost settings and seed as before. No tuning or model selection was performed on the test gameweeks. The full experiment contains eleven configurations (matched reduced, enriched full and nine group removals), each with 15 rounds and three models: 495 model fits. Twelve tests passed, covering the original time-ordering safeguards and new snapshot guards. The matched reduced rerun reproduced earlier predictions within numerical tolerance.','Upcoming fixtures, opponent statistics, fixture count and future fixture difficulty are still excluded. These 38 features are an enriched historical configuration, not the exact full production feature set. The production fixture bug is not repaired by this experiment.','## Updated prediction results','These are pooled errors over matched observations. Lower is better. Relative reduction compares enriched with reduced, not with the naive baseline.',table(['Metric','Reduced (16)','Enriched (38)','Error reduction'],rows),'Baseline definitions are unchanged: historical qualifying appearance mean for conditional points; five-round points mean; five-round participation frequency; and both five-round and previous-round minutes. Overall points remain conditional points multiplied by the probability of at least 30 minutes, omitting a separate short-appearance term.']
 cr=c[c.block_length==3];rows=[]
 for r in cr.itertuples():rows.append([labels[r.task],r.comparator,f'{r.mean_difference:.5f}',f'[{r.ci95_low:.5f}, {r.ci95_high:.5f}]',f'[{r.family_low:.5f}, {r.family_high:.5f}]'])
 text+=['The enriched model reduces pooled overall points MAE by about 4.25%, participation Brier error by 11.23%, and minutes MAE by 9.85% relative to the matched reduced model. Conditional points improves by only about 0.62%. In the adjusted primary intervals, the first three improvements remain below zero; the small conditional-points change is inconclusive. The enriched minutes model now shows a supported advantage over the five-round mean. Its MAE is still slightly higher than the previous-round baseline (12.184 versus 11.916), and their difference is uncertain.', '## Paired uncertainty','The estimand is equal-gameweek mean model loss minus comparator loss, so negative values favour the enriched model. It differs slightly from pooled row-weighted error. We use 100,000 circular block-bootstrap resamples, seed 20260915, primary block length three, and sensitivity lengths two and five. Whole gameweeks retain within-week dependence; blocks preserve some short-range temporal dependence.','The table shows marginal 95% intervals and wider Bonferroni-adjusted intervals across nine comparisons (five naive-baseline comparisons plus four matched-reduced comparisons). Coverage is approximate, particularly with only 15 weeks. Circular wrapping, temporal stability and dependence beyond the chosen blocks are assumptions. These are not independent-player tests, p-values or proof of future generalisation.',table(['Metric','Comparator','Difference','95% interval','Adjusted interval'],rows),'All sensitivity results and leave-one-week-out ranges are in analysis/comparison_uncertainty.csv. No refitting occurs inside the bootstrap; estimates condition on these predictions and do not cover training-seed or model-selection uncertainty.','## Feature-group ablations','Each group was removed from all three models and the complete temporal experiment repeated. All targets, rows and baselines were checked for equality. Positive ablated-minus-full loss means the group helps when the others remain. Related features can substitute for one another, so these are conditional contributions, not causal effects. Removing columns also changes the available feature space for the fixed training procedure.']
 rows=[]
 for name in ['full']+['without_'+n for n in meta['groups']]:rows.append([name]+[f'{get(name,t).mean_gameweek_loss:.5f}' for t in tasks])
 text.append(table(['Configuration']+[labels[t] for t in tasks],rows))
 text+=['The 36 exploratory comparisons (nine groups times four metrics) have their own Bonferroni family adjustment. These adjusted intervals are not simultaneous with the nine headline intervals as a single combined family. All block lengths and marginal/adjusted intervals appear in analysis/ablation_uncertainty.csv. We do not choose and deploy a winning ablation using these same evaluation rounds.','Availability is the clearest added contribution: removing status/chance information raises equal-gameweek overall points MAE by 0.03793, participation Brier by 0.00997 and minutes MAE by 1.34747. All three remain above zero in adjusted primary intervals. Removing market information also worsens overall points and minutes; removing position indicators worsens overall points. These are joint-group results, not evidence that every individual field independently helps.', 'ICT, API form and team strength have less conclusive incremental effects after adjustment. Recent points and minutes remain useful especially for minutes prediction. Conclusions from the old 16-feature ablations cannot simply be transferred because the newly available features provide overlapping information.', '## Diagnostics and charts']
 rows=[]
 for name,v in res['probability'].items():rows.append([name,f'{v["brier"]:.5f}',f'{v["auc"]:.5f}',f'{v["ece_10_bins"]:.5f}'])
 text+=[table(['Configuration','Brier','ROC-AUC','10-bin calibration gap'],rows),'Although Brier and ROC-AUC improve, the 10-bin calibration gap is slightly worse than the reduced model (0.01652 versus 0.01491). The highest enriched bin predicts 94.81% participation on average, compared with 89.61% observed (1,501 cases). Better discrimination and Brier do not imply every aspect of calibration improves. No recalibration is fitted on these evaluation folds.', 'The calibration gap is a sample-weighted absolute difference between predicted and observed participation in fixed 0.1-wide bins. Empty bins have zero counts. This descriptive value depends on binning and population and does not guarantee calibration for every probability range.',f'The population includes {res["nonplayers"]:,} zero-minute observations and {res["above90"]} observations above 90 minutes. {res["within2"]*100:.2f}% of overall points predictions are within two points, including non-players. Above-90 outcomes identify only some double gameweeks, not all special fixtures. No upper 90-minute prediction cap is used.','The regenerated charts cover points and minutes errors by gameweek; actual versus predicted averages; calibration with bin counts; scatter and error distributions; as-of position performance; coverage; ROC-AUC; and ablation intervals. Grouped tables cover actual/prior minutes, changed/unchanged minutes, history length, position, status and missing chance values. Largest-error examples are saved separately. Realised-minute groups are retrospective diagnostics, not groups perfectly identifiable before prediction.','## What still remains','The requested reruns with the recovered features are complete. The full production configuration still requires verified historical fixture/opponent inputs and a repair to future-fixture construction. Season-start/cold-start cases remain outside the five-consecutive-round eligibility rule. An untouched holdout has not been established: the historical corpus informed development. Scoring, recommendation, squad optimisation and technical chatbot evaluation remain separate stages. No production model, application behaviour or thesis chapter was changed.','## Evidence and sources','Source captures and their manifests are in ../historical-data-research/captures; exact feature rows and the run protocol are in this directory. Every configuration retains predictions and per-fold reports. analysis/ contains the recalculated metrics, intervals, calibration tables, diagnostics and ten charts. The analysis checks unique keys, matching labels/baselines, finite predictions and complete calibration counts.','[Archived FPL capture methodology](https://github.com/beeradb/FPL-Armband/blob/f8735a02e5c4abb018521f241340429c906d23ae/docs/backfill.md). [Block-bootstrap motivation](https://otexts.com/fpp3/bootstrap.html): our procedure resamples paired gameweek losses; it does not reproduce the source chapter\'s decomposition algorithm.']
 (R/'Updated-ML-Evaluation.md').write_text('\n\n'.join(text),encoding='utf-8')
 print('Updated report written')
if __name__=='__main__':main()
